<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 56 in Sept.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 56 in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index fell one point to 56 in September from 57 in August.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales fell to 60 in September from 61 in August. Traffic of prospective buyers fell to 43 from 46. The component index for single family sales in the next 6 months fell to 62 from 65, it said.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The September index is based on the ratings of 356 respondents.</p>
